{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1481436-scion-tales-of-heros","id":1481436,"title":"Scion: Tales of Heros","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-19T02:52:56-07:00","id":1481436,"title":"Scion: Tales of Heros","content":"Anyone else started reading this yet? Haven't finished it yet but so far I am pretty pleased with it, way more of the stories are hitting with me then missing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-19T19:56:10-07:00","id":1481509,"title":"","content":"So, its probably too late for this kind of thing and I'm not sure where I would even try to report it to, but there is an error in the story 'unconventional'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cYeah, blood quantum is a bitch,\u201d she recalled Jodie telling her. \u201cMy mom<br /> is half-blooded, but my father isn\u2019t part of the tribe, even though his own parents<br /> were. My own children won\u2019t qualify for tribal membership because white men<br /> are still trying to push us to extinction. Unless we get rid of the concept of blood<br /> quantum, we\u2019ve got maybe one or two generations before our whole band of the<br /> tribal council vanishes. As far as the rest of the council and I go, we would accept<br /> your application, Rowan. But I think you need to accept yourself, first.\u201d </div> </div> </div>Tribes are free to set their own membership qualifications and are under no obligation to follow the blood quantum methodology, they are not forced to use it by white people. In fact, since this story seems to be taking place in Michigan so far as I can tell, her local tribal government of the Ojibwe/Chippewa would be the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sault_Ste._Marie_Tribe_of_Chippewa_Indians_of_Michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Sault Ste. Marie Tribe of Chippewa Indians of Michigan</a>. One of the tribes that has <i>already </i>done away with the blood quantum concept as a membership requirement and would not deny membership to Jodie's father or her children in the described circumstance. Tribes that follow blood quantum methodology are doing so of their own free will because they decided they <i>wanted </i>a certain degree of racial purity as a membership requirement and the person complaining about it most likely isn't even a member of one of those tribes so its not going to be an issue to them in the manner described in the story. Before anyone asks, I'm familiar with the matter because I'm someone of native descent who learned this as part of a period where I was looking this kind of thing up (ended up not joining the tribe, though).<br /> <br /> Also, less sure here because I'm not as familiar on the matter, but since when did the Aesir worshiping nations of the past display the kind of aggressive expansionism that Theoi worshiping places like Rome did?<br /> <br /> Edit: And look, I get it, sometimes people make mistakes. I don't want people to think I'm being nitpicky over someone having a research fail. But earlier in the same story the author went out of their way to mock people that make that kind of research fail (the protagonist's roommate buys them a gift from a different tribe then she belongs to causing an aside reaming people who get that kind of thing wrong and think the tribes are all interchangeable) and once you write that kind of check I feel you have obligated yourself to cash it by getting things right yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 05-20-2022, 03:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-20T22:14:50-07:00","id":1481582,"title":"","content":"Well, finished it off. Overall I really like it, they mostly held up well and I feel like they gave me a good look into the setting of a modern world where all the myths are true+what it is like to be a scion. If I had to pick a favorite I'd say 'My Father's Daughter' was the best with its interesting idea of being a scion tasked with <u><i>stopping </i></u>heroes from invading the afterlife to bring a dead loved one back to life instead of being a hero that is trying to revive someone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member",